  "speaker": "Kṣemarāja (siddhāntin)",
  "question": "How is supreme Śiva — pure I-grasping — at once the thirty-sixfold expanse?",
  "premises": [
   "Ground: His essence full-I-grasping made of word-mass — Śiva Himself the 36-formed expanse.",
   "Word-mass: letter-heap a-to-ha enwombing all world; full I-grasp 'I alone light-selfed in shining,' freedom faceless.",
   "Definition: tattva = the one undivided shining causing divided classes' classing (hill-earth, river-water).",
   "List: the thirty-six names in order, bare."
  ],
  "inference": "Phonemic fullness grounds plurality; undivided shine families the divided; roll bare.",
  "uncertainties": [
   "List bare here; marks follow in p07–p08 (promissory structure).",
   "śabdarāśi assumes mātṛkā doctrine without exposition."
